SELECT
CustomerID,
COUNT(OrderID) AS OrderCount,
SUM(TotalSales) AS Revenue
FROM Sales
GROUP BY CustomerID
HAVING COUNT(OrderID) > 1
ORDER BY OrderCount DESC;

Customer loyalty plays a critical role in business success. Loyal customers remain committed to a brand and its products despite price adjustments.

SELECT
c.Region,
COUNT(DISTINCT s.CustomerID) AS Customers,
SUM(s.TotalSales) AS Revenue,
SUM(s.Profit) AS Profit
FROM Sales s
JOIN Customers c
ON s.CustomerID = c.CustomerID
GROUP BY c.Region
ORDER BY Revenue DESC;

Profit is generated across different regions enabling the business to allocate products based on regional demand and maximize profitability.

SELECT
Channel,
COUNT(OrderID) AS TotalOrders,
SUM(TotalSales) AS Revenue,
SUM(Profit) AS Profit
FROM Sales
GROUP BY Channel;

The majority of the company's sales revenue is generated through online purchases, providing an opportunity to capitalize on the growing e-commerce market. This enables the business to drive revenue growth while minimizing the significant costs associated with investing in and maintaining physical store locations.

